GRA-11  Harwell-Boeing loader indexes verttax with unchecked row index / column pointers
  Inputs are generated by gen_hb.py (python3 -I gen_hb.py .); generated copies are included.
  <build>/bin/gcv -ib bad99.hb /dev/null        (row index 99 in a 4x4 matrix)
  <build>/bin/gcv -ib bad0.hb  /dev/null        (blank field -> decoded 0)
  <build>/bin/gcv -ib badn1.hb out.grf          (row index n+1; then gtst out.grf)
  <build>/bin/gcv -ib baddec.hb out.grf         (decreasing column pointers; then gtst out.grf)
  <build>/bin/gcv -ib badcol.hb out.grf         (column pointer 99)
7.0.17 : bad99/bad0 -> AddressSanitizer heap-buffer-overflow READ in graphGeomLoadHabo.
7.0.18 pristine (0ef275a0): bad99 and bad0 are rejected ("bad input (9)"); badcol is rejected
  ("bad input (8)", by luck of the EOF test); badn1 still loads through gcv and the converted
  graph is rejected by gtst ("invalid number of edges"); baddec loads and the converted graph
  passes gtst although arcs were silently dropped.
Series (0007): bad99/bad0/badn1 -> "bad input (9)", badcol/baddec -> "bad input (10)";
  ok.hb still loads. hbpart.c loads, checks and partitions a file through the C library.
